{"question_text": {"৪৯তম বিসিএস ⎯ ফলিত গণিত (৫৬১)": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) Which of the following is true about motion in a resting medium?", "option1": "Relative velocity depends on the motion of the medium", "option2": "The medium does not affect the motion", "option3": "Velocity of the object = velocity of medium", "option4": "Both (b) and (c)", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p> Since the medium is at rest, it doesn’t alter the motion. Velocity is directly the object’s velocity relative to the medium</p>"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Which term in the spherical polar expression for velocity represents the azimuthal motion?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_221546347.png\" width=\"66\" height=\"55\" alt=\"\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_221803115.png\" width=\"129\" height=\"47\" alt=\"\">", "option3": "<span id=\"mce_1_start\"><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_221654491.png\" width=\"130\" height=\"39\" alt=\"\"></span>", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_221729860.png\" width=\"122\" height=\"49\" alt=\"\">", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_222022530.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"574\" height=\"187\"></p>"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_EeyFtWy.png\" width=\"849\" height=\"42\" alt=\"\">", "option1": "Radial motion", "option2": "Circular motion in a plane", "option3": "Linear motion along z-axis", "option4": "Oscillatory motion", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><br>​<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_222623065.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"766\" height=\"205\"></p>"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) The squared speed v<sup>2</sup> in spherical coordinates equals", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_223140285.png\" width=\"276\" height=\"56\" alt=\"\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_223215098.png\" width=\"310\" height=\"41\" alt=\"\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_223258326.png\" width=\"202\" height=\"57\" alt=\"\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_223326230.png\" width=\"223\" height=\"48\" alt=\"\">", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_223510491.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"598\" height=\"38\"><br>​Dot product of v vector.<br>​</p>"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) An airplane flies at 200 km/h in still air. How long will it take to cover 400 km?", "option1": "1 hour", "option2": "1.5 hours", "option3": "2 hours", "option4": "3 hours", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_095545932.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"274\" height=\"56\"></p>"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) A stone is thrown horizontally with a speed of 20 m/s from the top of a tower of height 80 m. Find the horizontal range. (g=10 m/s<sup>2</sup>)", "option1": "80 m", "option2": "100 m", "option3": "120 m", "option4": "160 m", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_100731571.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"401\" height=\"184\"></p>"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) A projectile is fired at an angle of 45° with an initial velocity of 20 m/s in still air. What is the time of flight?(Take g=10 m/s<sup>2</sup>)", "option1": "2 s", "option2": "2√2 s", "option3": "4√2 s", "option4": "5 s", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_101033830.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"523\" height=\"76\"> </p>"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) For motion constrained to r = R (constant), the radial acceleration is:", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_224554963.png\" width=\"162\" height=\"47\" alt=\"\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_224629844.png\" width=\"154\" height=\"46\" alt=\"\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_224704374.png\" width=\"320\" height=\"44\" alt=\"\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_224835695.png\" width=\"304\" height=\"51\" alt=\"\">", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_224921980.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"407\" height=\"78\"></p>"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) Let r(t) = 2t, θ(t) = π/4​ (constant), Φ(t) = t<sup>2</sup>. At t = 1, the speed is&nbsp;", "option1": "2", "option2": "2√2​", "option3": "2√3", "option4": "12", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_225437518.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"589\" height=\"122\"></p>"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) A particle is moving in a resting medium with constant velocity <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_BpI69bF.png\" width=\"123\" height=\"42\" alt=\"\">&nbsp;m/s. What will be the displacement after 5 seconds?", "option1": "30 m", "option2": "25 m", "option3": "20 m", "option4": "15 m", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_101534041.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"314\" height=\"129\"></p>"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) Under a central force <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_230047704.png\" width=\"134\" height=\"47\" alt=\"\"> , which θ-equation of motion is correct?", "option1": "<span id=\"mce_1_start\"><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_230205487.png\" width=\"381\" height=\"37\" alt=\"\"></span>", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_230243215.png\" width=\"397\" height=\"37\" alt=\"\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_230331052.png\" width=\"181\" height=\"37\" alt=\"\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_230405490.png\" width=\"183\" height=\"35\" alt=\"\">", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_230449096.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"781\" height=\"102\"><br>​θ component = transverse component.</p>"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) A particle moves such that its position at time t is <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_231450803.png\" width=\"327\" height=\"53\" alt=\"\">What is its acceleration <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_6bstLZ1.png\" width=\"138\" height=\"39\" alt=\"\">", "option1": "8i", "option2": "8i + 3j", "option3": "4i", "option4": "0", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_231938259.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"508\" height=\"91\"></p>"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_erqgDCC.png\" width=\"932\" height=\"85\" alt=\"\">", "option1": "2 m/s", "option2": "8.5 m/s", "option3": "10.2 m/s", "option4": "11.7 m/s", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_232856971.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"454\" height=\"317\"></p>", "is_audio": true, "question_duration": "00:17", "answer_duration": "00:04", "explain_duration": "00:00"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) <span id=\"mce_1_start\"><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_0dtJdYM.png\" width=\"990\" height=\"102\" alt=\"\"><br></span>", "option1": "21 m/s<sup>2</sup>", "option2": "-21 m/s<sup>2</sup>", "option3": "19 m/s<sup>2</sup>", "option4": "-19 m/s<sup>2</sup>", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_234440433.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"342\" height=\"65\"><br>​<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_234621162.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"354\" height=\"248\"></p>"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_102352379.png\" width=\"508\" height=\"42\" alt=\"\">", "option1": "0.25 s", "option2": "0.5 s", "option3": "1 s", "option4": "2 s", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_102549957.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"728\" height=\"46\"></p>"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) A particle has position in Cartesian form:<br>x(t) = t<sup>2</sup>, y(t) = 2t, z(t) = 3t. Find its speed at t = 2.", "option1": "√68m/s", "option2": "√29m/s", "option3": "9m/s", "option4": "14m/s", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_235049216.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"446\" height=\"220\"></p>"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) A particle has position:<br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_235544784.png\" width=\"388\" height=\"56\" alt=\"\">Find its acceleration at t = 2.", "option1": "0", "option2": "8i + 8j + 10k", "option3": "6i + 4j + 0k", "option4": "12i + 4j", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_235651501.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"350\" height=\"160\"></p>"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_102839029.png\" width=\"373\" height=\"74\" alt=\"\">", "option1": "13/12", "option2": "0", "option3": "1", "option4": "3", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_103300060.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"562\" height=\"46\"></p>"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) A particle moves such that r = 4, θ = π/3, Φ = t, with all in SI units. Find the radial acceleration.", "option1": "3", "option2": "-3", "option3": "0", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-20_002106693.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"198\" height=\"44\"><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-20_002206362.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"350\" height=\"144\"></p>"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-20_003505541.png\" width=\"498\" height=\"62\" alt=\"\"><br>Final acceleration:", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-20_003642903.png\" width=\"324\" height=\"50\" alt=\"\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-20_003722534.png\" width=\"298\" height=\"50\" alt=\"\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-20_003804959.png\" width=\"207\" height=\"38\" alt=\"\">", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-20_003908667.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"239\" height=\"65\"></p>"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) In Cartesian coordinates, the velocity of a particle with position vector<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_220741868.png\" width=\"376\" height=\"41\" alt=\"\"> is :", "option1": "<span id=\"mce_1_start\"><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_220907036.png\" width=\"272\" height=\"43\" alt=\"\"></span>", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_220935036.png\" width=\"276\" height=\"42\" alt=\"\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_221007252.png\" width=\"258\" height=\"42\" alt=\"\">", "option4": "None if these", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-19_221057519.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"522\" height=\"131\"></p>"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) A particle is thrown with velocity u = 20 m/s at angle 30° in calm air. Find its horizontal velocity after 2 s.", "option1": "20 ms", "option2": "10 ms", "option3": "17.3", "option4": "0", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-20_033335496.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"646\" height=\"142\"></p>"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) Buoyant force acting on a body submerged in a fluid is equal to:", "option1": "Mass of displaced fluid", "option2": "Volume of displaced fluid", "option3": "Weight of displaced fluid", "option4": "Weight of body", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p>Archimedes’ principle: Buoyant force = weight of displaced fluid.</p>"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) A body falling in a fluid attains terminal velocity because:", "option1": "Weight becomes zero", "option2": "Buoyancy becomes zero", "option3": "Net force on the body becomes zero due to drag balancing weight and buoyancy", "option4": "Its mass increases", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p>At terminal velocity, weight = buoyancy + drag, so acceleration becomes zero.</p>"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) A particle’s position vector is <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-20_054401788.png\" width=\"365\" height=\"54\" alt=\"\">The path is:", "option1": "Straight line in XY-plane", "option2": "Circle in XY-plane", "option3": "Parabola in XY-plane", "option4": "Spiral in 3D", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-20_054612071.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"228\" height=\"115\"></p>"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) A particle in spherical coordinates has: r = 1, θ = π/2​, Φ = t. Find its speed at t = 2.", "option1": "1", "option2": "√2", "option3": "2", "option4": "0", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-20_054247998.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"396\" height=\"179\"></p>"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) A particle moves such that its velocity is always along vector&nbsp;<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_lkJBjUl.png\" width=\"153\" height=\"47\" alt=\"\"><span></span><span>What is the nature of its trajectory?</span>", "option1": "Circular path", "option2": "Straight line in XY-plane", "option3": "Parabola in XY-plane", "option4": "Spiral in 3D", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-20_053755919.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"452\" height=\"200\"></p>"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) A particle moves in the plane with polar coordinates: r(t) = 2t, θ(t) = t<sup>2</sup>.Find the speed v at t=1 s.", "option1": "√5", "option2": "2√5", "option3": "3√5", "option4": "4√5", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-20_053035753.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"539\" height=\"276\"></p>"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) In motion with linear drag F = - kv, the time constant τ = m/k​ physically represents:", "option1": "Time to reach terminal velocity exactly", "option2": "Time after which velocity becomes zero", "option3": "Characteristic time to reduce velocity by factor 1/e", "option4": "Time taken to double the velocity", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-20_052220240.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"738\" height=\"319\"></p>"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) Reynolds number is a ratio of:", "option1": "Viscous force to inertial force", "option2": "Inertial force to viscous force", "option3": "Buoyant force to viscous force", "option4": "Weight to drag force", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-20_051625432.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"370\" height=\"111\"></p>"}]}, "_source": "archive-question-subject", "_exam_id": 12096, "custom_field": "প্রতি প্রশ্নের মান ১ ও ভুল উত্তরের জন্য ০.৫০ কাটা যাবে।", "exam_time": "1800000", "is_omr": true, "omr_time": "2100000", "examname": "Aug 21, 2025", "type": "Math-Sub-561-applied", "payment": "BALANCE_NOT"}